    "report": "The archive feature is finished and committed as `7010cce` on `main`, the current branch. I did not push.\n\n**What I added on top of the previous developer's work** (their commit `1e0c213` already had the domain behaviour, the handler, the storage and a domain spec):\n- **Route:** `POST /conversations/:id/archive`, answered with `acceptCommand` like `read`.\n- **Controller and wiring:** the controller method, and the handler registered once in `module.local.ts`. Before this, the handler existed but nothing called it.\n- **`GET /conversations/mine`:** the summary read model gets an `archived` flag, computed in SQL against the reader's archive and the latest message. Only `mine` filters on it, so a new message brings the conversation back and re-archiving changes nothing.\n- **`GET /conversations/unread`:** unchanged, so archived conversations still count.\n- **Tests:** three e2e tests covering the list, unread, re-archive, the message that brings it back, refusal to a stranger, and 401 when signed out.\n\n**Verification**\n- `yarn typecheck`: clean.\n- Unit tests: 148 suites, 1014 tests pass.\n- Full e2e: 114 suites, 610 tests pass.\n- `yarn check:conventions`, eslint and prettier on the changed files: clean.\n\n**Choices and things to know**\n- The refusal for a non-reader is `ConversationNotVisible` through the operation's `ERROR`, the same as `read`. That is how the existing commands refuse a conversation the caller cannot see.\n- The previous developer's `isArchivedBy` is only called from the domain spec. The list uses the SQL flag instead, so the domain method is unused in production code. I left it in place because it documents the rule.\n- You asked for the commit on the current branch, which is `main`. The shared guidance says to branch first when on the default branch. I followed your instruction; if you want a branch instead, it is a one-command change.\n- I did not start a server, so port 4471 was not used.",
